WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.125
Step 1: Complete the location’s current Fast Food Award setup. New and edited shifts automatically receive a break plan when saved; inline card edits use the normal autosave. Existing published rosters and approved timesheets are preserved.

2
00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:25.833
Step 2: Open the shift’s dollar icon and choose Breaks. Automatic shows the planned paid 10-minute rests and unpaid meals with 12-hour times. The standard meal is 30 minutes; counts and timing follow working hours, five-hour limits and recorded part-time meals.

3
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:39.542
Step 3: Change the shift start or finish in Details, then review the updated Breaks preview. Paid rests remain paid. Shorter shifts remove unneeded meals; longer shifts add the required breaks. Save shift applies popup changes and recalculates the roster estimate.

4
00:00:39.542 --> 00:00:53.542
Step 4: For a permitted adjustment, choose Custom and edit the planned times or durations. Owed breaks, first/last-hour limits, separate rest and meal breaks, and part-time agreement times are checked before saving. Record an agreed written variation when changing an agreed meal.

5
00:00:53.542 --> 00:01:07.542
Step 5: Review any planning issue before saving or publishing. A recorded meal that cannot fit the shift needs an agreement review. Adjacent cards forming one continuous engagement must be combined for automatic planning. Unresolved plans never claim a complete wage estimate.

6
00:01:07.542 --> 00:01:20.917
Step 6: Publish the reviewed week. Staff can expand Planned breaks on their published roster, including on phones. Staff must still clock actual breaks when taken: plans do not create clock events or automatically deduct unpaid time from actual work.
